#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid "2D Graphs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add a new 2D graph on &kalgebra;, what you have to do is to go to the "
"<guilabel>2D Graph</guilabel> tab and click in the <guilabel>Add</guilabel> "
"tab to add the new function. Then your focus will go to an input text box "
"where you can type your function."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to use a typical f(x) function it is not necessary to specify "
"it, but if you want a f(y) or a polar function, you will have to add y-> and "
"q-> as the bounded variables."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid "sin(x)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>x²</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid "y->sin(y)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid "q->3*sin(7q)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid "q=0..100->q"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have entered the function click on the <guibutton>OK</guibutton> "
"button to display the graph in the main window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid "Features"
msgstr "Foncions"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:225
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can set several graphs on the same view. Just use the <guilabel>Add</"
"guilabel> button when you are in List mode. You can set each graph its own "
"color."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The view can be zoomed and moved with the mouse. Using the wheel you can "
"zoom in and out. You can also select an area with the left button of the "
"mouse and this area will be zoomed in."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>List</guilabel> tab, you can open a context menu with a "
"&RMB; click on a function and hide or remove it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid "3D Graphs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To draw a 3D Graph with &kalgebra; you will have to go to the <guilabel>3D "
"Graph</guilabel> tab and you will see an input field at the bottom where you "
"will type your function. For the moment &kalgebra; only supports functions "
"that fit f(x,y) that will define the Z."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid "sin(x)*sin(y)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>x/y</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid "Dictionary"
msgstr "Diccionari"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The dictionary is a collection of all &kalgebra; available operations. It "
"can be useful to check in the dictionary what is an operation useful for and "
"to know how many parameters does a function stand for."
msgstr ""

